From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emir Beganovic <beganovic.emir@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 11:25:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: x1e80100: raise the Zenbook 14 UX3480QA digital
 speaker ceiling to 0 dB

The upstream -3 dB digital cap (81) holds a full-scale signal 3 dB short
of the WSA884x amplifiers' full scale. On the ASUS Zenbook 14 (UX3480QA)
the speakers were noticeably quiet even at 100% volume, and raising the
WSA RX Digital Volume ceiling to 84 (0 dB), the value the upstream UCM
requests, gave the full +3.1 dB cleanly: measured with the built-in
DMICs at 600 Hz, output tracked input dB for dB from -20 dBFS up to
0 dBFS with no PA faults, and 800 Hz - 10 kHz stayed below 0.5% THD at
-6 dBFS.

Its PA Volume is left at the upstream 0 dB cap (6): on this board PA
Volume does not change the output at all (measured within 0.04 dB across
PA 1, 3 and 6, and within 0.01 dB with the compander off), so raising
that cap would buy nothing.

Signed-off-by: Emir Beganovic <beganovic.emir@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c | 11 ++++++-----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c	2026-11-28 10:23:18.018960350 +0000
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c	2026-11-28 10:23:18.041661726 +0000
@@ -48,10 +48,11 @@
 		 * its amplifiers' OCP, PBR and thermal protection (the wsa884x
 		 * 2S/4 ohm profile) are relied on instead.
 		 *
-		 * The ASUS Zenbook A16 gets the 0 dB digital ceiling only. Its
-		 * PA Volume does not change the output, so raising that cap
-		 * would buy nothing; the digital cap was what held a full-scale
-		 * signal 3 dB short of the amplifiers' full scale.
+		 * The ASUS Zenbook A16 and Zenbook 14 (UX3480QA) get the 0 dB
+		 * digital ceiling only. Their PA Volume does not change the
+		 * output, so raising that cap would buy nothing; the digital
+		 * cap was what held a full-scale signal 3 dB short of the
+		 * amplifiers' full scale.
 		 *
 		 * The Samsung Galaxy Book4 Edge 14 has WSA883x amplifiers, whose
 		 * PA Volume steps differ: 6 is -3 dB there and 17 is 0 dB, the
@@ -61,7 +62,8 @@
 		if (of_machine_is_compatible("microsoft,denali")) {
 			digital_max = 84;
 			pa_max = 12;
-		} else if (of_machine_is_compatible("asus,zenbook-a16-ux3607oa")) {
+		} else if (of_machine_is_compatible("asus,zenbook-a16-ux3607oa") ||
+			   of_machine_is_compatible("asus,zenbook-14-ux3480qa")) {
 			digital_max = 84;
 			pa_max = 6;
 		} else if (of_machine_is_compatible("samsung,galaxy-book4-edge-14")) {
